theory.intro:
**Average speed** is the total distance travelled divided by the total time taken. On a distance–time graph where distance records cumulative distance travelled, it is the gradient of the straight line joining the start and end of the journey. On a height or position graph, the endpoint gradient gives signed average change; for an object falling without reversing direction, use the distance fallen divided by the time taken.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.9,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.2) node[above] {$d$};
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,0) -- (2,2.4) -- (3.2,2.4) -- (5,4.4);
\node[above,font=\small] at (2.6,2.45) {stopped};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0,0) -- (5,4.4) node[pos=0.75,above left,font=\small] {average speed};
\fill (0,0) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (5,4.4) circle (2.5pt);
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.9,2.6) {Distance};
\node[below] at (2.9,-0.9) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
The graph records a cyclist's cumulative distance travelled. Find the average speed over the whole journey, including the stop.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{journeyBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,black] (0,0) -- (5.6,0) node[right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$t$ (h)};
\draw[->,black] (0,0) -- (0,4.7) node[above,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$d$ (km)};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw[black] (\x,0.08) -- (\x,-0.08); \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.08) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\v in {1/12,2/24,3/36,4/48} {\draw[black] (-0.08,\y) -- (0.08,\y); \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.08,\y) {$\v$};}
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[very thick,journeyBlue] (0,0) -- (2,2) -- (3,2) -- (5,4);
\foreach \x/\y in {0/0,2/2,3/2,5/4} {\fill[black] (\x,\y) circle (2pt);}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
The horizontal segment records a stop from $t=2$ to $t=3\text{ h}$. This hour counts in the total time.

$\begin{aligned}\text{Average speed}&=\dfrac{\Delta d}{\Delta t}\\&=\dfrac{48-0}{5-0}\\&=9.6\text{ km/h}\end{aligned}$

This is the gradient of the secant joining the journey's endpoints.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{journeyBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{secantRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[->,black] (0,0) -- (5.6,0) node[right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$t$ (h)};
\draw[->,black] (0,0) -- (0,4.7) node[above,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$d$ (km)};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw[black] (\x,0.08) -- (\x,-0.08); \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.08) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\v in {1/12,2/24,3/36,4/48} {\draw[black] (-0.08,\y) -- (0.08,\y); \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.08,\y) {$\v$};}
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[very thick,journeyBlue] (0,0) -- (2,2) -- (3,2) -- (5,4);
\draw[thick,dashed,secantRed] (0,0) -- (5,4);
\foreach \x/\y in {0/0,2/2,3/2,5/4} {\fill[black] (\x,\y) circle (2pt);}
\path (2.5,2) node[above,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] {stopped};
\path (3.7,2.96) node[below right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=secantRed] {secant};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
The distance–time graph records a car's cumulative distance travelled at constant speed. Find its average speed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{journeyBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,black] (0,0) -- (5,0) node[right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$t$ (h)};
\draw[->,black] (0,0) -- (0,4.8) node[above,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$d$ (km)};
\foreach \x/\v in {1/0.5,2/1,3/1.5,4/2} {\draw[black] (\x,0.08) -- (\x,-0.08); \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.08) {$\v$};}
\foreach \y/\v in {1/30,2/60,3/90,4/120} {\draw[black] (-0.08,\y) -- (0.08,\y); \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.08,\y) {$\v$};}
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[very thick,journeyBlue] (0,0) -- (4,4);
\fill[black] (4,4) circle (2pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
The distance–time graph shows a car travelling along a highway.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.5,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$d$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/50,2/100,3/150,4/200,5/250} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,0) -- (4,4.0);
\fill (4,4.0) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above left,font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (4,4.0) {$(4,200)$};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,2.75) {Distance (km)};
\node[below] at (2.7,-0.9) {Time (h)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the average speed of the car over the $4\text{-hour}$ journey.

The graph shows a cyclist's journey, which includes a rest stop.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.5,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$d$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/15,2/30,3/45,4/60,5/75} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,0) -- (2,2.0) -- (3,2.0) -- (5,4.0);
\fill (0,0) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (2,2.0) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (3,2.0) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (5,4.0) circle (2.5pt);
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,2.75) {Distance (km)};
\node[below] at (2.7,-0.9) {Time (h)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Calculate the cyclist's average speed for the entire $5\text{-hour}$ trip.

